# Testing Standards

Testing work must follow the Spec Registry:

- `specs/README.md`
- `specs/security/SEC-002-security-testing.md`

Mandatory testing expectations:

- every feature implementation should include matching tests unless the change is documentation-only;
- security-sensitive changes require attack-path tests, not only happy-path tests;
- backend tests must cover auth, RBAC, ownership, tenant isolation and validation boundaries;
- frontend tests must cover routing, critical states and unsafe rendering protections when relevant;
- regressions from bugs or incidents must include a reproducible failing test before closure;
- mocks must not contain real credentials, customer secrets or production data.
